{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voices": [
    "en-US-AndrewNeural"
  ],
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "17",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m11p17-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "5e155a028c08c5fda394f334035c2ba3ab4a0934d9d21e93224156fe3f5201af",
        "2": "c205d095a8f77c751d9b9c182297a4cf34d336cbd62549a4a1ecc982c21d8e81",
        "3": "6e8b91de3b54a178f306b4fcf26d26d4e6491db3f012437314978278e543dca5",
        "4": "b6a6ebc8280786a3a375e280cd4290f011d0e58adc0f16f3782003c1865b0a23"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s01-c1-2b137866953d",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The app keeps asking for the same result. A cache hit gives it that result without repeating the database work. On a miss, the app loads the authoritative value and fills the cache for another request.",
          "text_sha256": "2b137866953db96a8283d5fa7cc22cee94ca6f3717107c582d5c09c460b306e0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2b137866953db96a8283d5fa7cc22cee94ca6f3717107c582d5c09c460b306e0",
          "asset_sha256": "5e155a028c08c5fda394f334035c2ba3ab4a0934d9d21e93224156fe3f5201af"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s01-c2-508e9d6a832a",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose an engine for the operations the app needs, then choose serverless or node-based for how you want to run it. Decide how cache keys expire and how the app handles data that's no longer there.",
          "text_sha256": "508e9d6a832acf5e563574ba45e5e7a9d72f753e8b9be991d3dc015eb7b31b63",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "508e9d6a832acf5e563574ba45e5e7a9d72f753e8b9be991d3dc015eb7b31b63",
          "asset_sha256": "5e155a028c08c5fda394f334035c2ba3ab4a0934d9d21e93224156fe3f5201af"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s02-c1-246d4f204daf",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the app already sends supported Dynamo D B item or query operations, dacks can cache on that read path. Dynamo D B is still the authoritative store.",
          "text_sha256": "246d4f204daf2ec45f6638f249aa024fe0f3d1f866d7d7041ef67cc4851ad0d8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "25bdaea2d439c95bdd37d1c9c8eb70a542c3c3693c3631400f661fab445d1e96",
          "asset_sha256": "c205d095a8f77c751d9b9c182297a4cf34d336cbd62549a4a1ecc982c21d8e81"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s02-c2-6093ce33fa7e",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Suppose the value is a calculated total or a session. With Elastic Cache, the app designs the key and the value, then decides when to expire or invalidate it. dacks does not do that application work for you.",
          "text_sha256": "6093ce33fa7ea94353b28c03e475291d8511a86976fbf5c2ebffb00dd056add6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "01900cb79e528f27f63cdc05103bae5298184868a3a8671fe5838581efe207f5",
          "asset_sha256": "c205d095a8f77c751d9b9c182297a4cf34d336cbd62549a4a1ecc982c21d8e81"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s03-c1-4a27a0971f7c",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The app checks the cache before opening the database path. If it finds a usable value, it returns that directly.",
          "text_sha256": "4a27a0971f7ca0e0e91a3b6cadb02b6731b8f89cb3122f5815f5080631e2bb0c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4a27a0971f7ca0e0e91a3b6cadb02b6731b8f89cb3122f5815f5080631e2bb0c",
          "asset_sha256": "6e8b91de3b54a178f306b4fcf26d26d4e6491db3f012437314978278e543dca5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s03-c2-9457ed90cdb1",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Now make the same request after expiry. The app reads the source, puts the result back into the cache with a lifetime, and returns it. The source must still handle that miss.",
          "text_sha256": "9457ed90cdb15dfc6b231d3e01d6a7d3bc02622cc078fec42ac512da6fe3e424",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9457ed90cdb15dfc6b231d3e01d6a7d3bc02622cc078fec42ac512da6fe3e424",
          "asset_sha256": "6e8b91de3b54a178f306b4fcf26d26d4e6491db3f012437314978278e543dca5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s03-c3-7859656b25d5",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "What if many requests miss for the same key at once? Coalesce the work, use bounded retries and jitter where appropriate, and monitor actual database load. A high cache hit rate alone does not describe that failure path.",
          "text_sha256": "7859656b25d560db03881b55597fbd4e6ab43668e5198ecccd16f6592f437562",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7859656b25d560db03881b55597fbd4e6ab43668e5198ecccd16f6592f437562",
          "asset_sha256": "6e8b91de3b54a178f306b4fcf26d26d4e6491db3f012437314978278e543dca5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s04-c1-90c09812f63c",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "An update changes the authoritative record. Invalidate or refresh the cache according to the design so a later reader can see the new value. Decide what happens if that cache action fails.",
          "text_sha256": "90c09812f63c2529ff032b51ba4332241e7da713894e0285ab63ad32f616c66a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "90c09812f63c2529ff032b51ba4332241e7da713894e0285ab63ad32f616c66a",
          "asset_sha256": "b6a6ebc8280786a3a375e280cd4290f011d0e58adc0f16f3782003c1865b0a23"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s04-c2-08bf65ecadf4",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "A slower read may have fetched the old value before the write. If it fills the cache after invalidation, the old value can come back. Invalidating once doesn't, by itself, remove that race.",
          "text_sha256": "08bf65ecadf44be29ca8d9c80a8b530f521c2efa02019c6f486bda83abb20d89",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "08bf65ecadf44be29ca8d9c80a8b530f521c2efa02019c6f486bda83abb20d89",
          "asset_sha256": "b6a6ebc8280786a3a375e280cd4290f011d0e58adc0f16f3782003c1865b0a23"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p17-andrew-exp-s04-c3-c2d791fd39a0",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "A time to live limits how long a cached entry lingers; it does not make reads instantly correct. Use version-aware keys, coordination, or a source read for decisions that cannot tolerate the stale value.",
          "text_sha256": "c2d791fd39a0f4b7bf0695cac4af3dedc1b74fc18ddf27d579ba3301e9d4f6ed",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c2d791fd39a0f4b7bf0695cac4af3dedc1b74fc18ddf27d579ba3301e9d4f6ed",
          "asset_sha256": "b6a6ebc8280786a3a375e280cd4290f011d0e58adc0f16f3782003c1865b0a23"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "18",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m11p18-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "4729ed2b395bdc376692635d1b48732979ae2205204830abc686759631bea707",
        "2": "da6fc93c9ac663ad80e842f9386edf76c8d08e9e68d6d07fa5d9c9025552b236",
        "3": "fb4236df309206087222b0200ecfe9d9233518033c83e159a594e2f2049d296c",
        "4": "230c3d7994306eab379341bdc4f42bbec3c9d8a7868b7eddc8b027589a9ab87d"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s01-c1-06f0eecc010d",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The cookie carries a session identifier. The load balancer can send the next request to either server, and each can look up the authorized session in the shared store. Replacing one server doesn't have to discard the session.",
          "text_sha256": "06f0eecc010deced8aab5bcd65735b23cc6f020da699eaf7e01f7a33019e06fb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "06f0eecc010deced8aab5bcd65735b23cc6f020da699eaf7e01f7a33019e06fb",
          "asset_sha256": "4729ed2b395bdc376692635d1b48732979ae2205204830abc686759631bea707"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s01-c2-7c50e7a974fe",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The identifier needs protection in transit and at the client. Plan what happens if an entry expires or is evicted. The app may need the user to sign in again instead of claiming a lost session still exists.",
          "text_sha256": "7c50e7a974fe58dd6f54a46e0b5f882fe68f30b164c518470de53d891b6c01b4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7c50e7a974fe58dd6f54a46e0b5f882fe68f30b164c518470de53d891b6c01b4",
          "asset_sha256": "4729ed2b395bdc376692635d1b48732979ae2205204830abc686759631bea707"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s02-c1-7ecb55dca19e",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the app needs hashes, sets or sorted sets, evaluate Valkey or Redis O S S. Check replication, failover and backup support for the exact version and deployment.",
          "text_sha256": "7ecb55dca19e2a1ab74f720007a7c2d13ab19d2755ff72cc644edb0f0cab9887",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9ea5c0136bacbbff01e9771d6789242e59dcdcdc55e8417f09b9edb933aa9706",
          "asset_sha256": "da6fc93c9ac663ad80e842f9386edf76c8d08e9e68d6d07fa5d9c9025552b236"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s02-c2-8ee63b0842b3",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For simple disposable values, mem cashed can fit. The traditional node-based design shards data across nodes; it does not inherit the other engines' replication behavior.",
          "text_sha256": "8ee63b0842b3d817f47c767a87944a1b0b1f855aa49421f1462909c00bba5864",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b580fdb438000906c15ef1b18e66dc546fcec742a56fea665db33317e7ce513c",
          "asset_sha256": "da6fc93c9ac663ad80e842f9386edf76c8d08e9e68d6d07fa5d9c9025552b236"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s02-c3-316ec3844863",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Do not generalize the node-based rules to serverless. For example, serverless mem cashed supports snapshots. Check the actual operating model before treating one engine name as a complete feature list.",
          "text_sha256": "316ec3844863ed352440e115a526a11f937f8895134750ba93cf7a393863d313",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "680e792b670ae142ac0aa8137c89d1c632469a915403bfb6cd986dcf6ae2490c",
          "asset_sha256": "da6fc93c9ac663ad80e842f9386edf76c8d08e9e68d6d07fa5d9c9025552b236"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s03-c1-4bd92ab2e6f2",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Shard keys to spread capacity and traffic. If one key stays unusually hot, adding shards does not automatically spread requests for that individual key.",
          "text_sha256": "4bd92ab2e6f2549d1ec8f5afe21e3e7d23ec12fde38f0efcf25a680883d4f882",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4bd92ab2e6f2549d1ec8f5afe21e3e7d23ec12fde38f0efcf25a680883d4f882",
          "asset_sha256": "fb4236df309206087222b0200ecfe9d9233518033c83e159a594e2f2049d296c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s03-c2-bcc243c7391b",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A primary and replica can support failover in a suitable configuration. Replication moves data between live nodes; it does not give you a retained recovery point for an earlier mistake.",
          "text_sha256": "bcc243c7391bb41aa6478eed61b40e8bbbf3812f9655b775a2cbd3c285014a58",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bcc243c7391bb41aa6478eed61b40e8bbbf3812f9655b775a2cbd3c285014a58",
          "asset_sha256": "fb4236df309206087222b0200ecfe9d9233518033c83e159a594e2f2049d296c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s03-c3-1f0baa0f05b4",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Where supported, take a snapshot and rehearse a restore. Save authoritative data independently. Successful failover does not prove a past value can be recovered.",
          "text_sha256": "1f0baa0f05b4d803dc99e877db325869fe72736fbd7aaf8ab3d106f3c0383fb0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1f0baa0f05b4d803dc99e877db325869fe72736fbd7aaf8ab3d106f3c0383fb0",
          "asset_sha256": "fb4236df309206087222b0200ecfe9d9233518033c83e159a594e2f2049d296c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s04-c1-283dda327067",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "A burst hits the app. Is it cache misses, A P I limits, compute, connections, the database write path, or key usage? Follow the request through each layer. A fast edge cache cannot fix a saturated database write partition.",
          "text_sha256": "283dda3270676175a64bb1e67c13d8e058a7139141e6a846e93c3f4925bc2eed",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6c0c89616f51c6e68d731a5c0511e0ff8a1aab7192586994a49f2676846a18bd",
          "asset_sha256": "230c3d7994306eab379341bdc4f42bbec3c9d8a7868b7eddc8b027589a9ab87d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p18-andrew-exp-s04-c2-28d6296c8dd6",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Check actual request rate, work in flight, item size and cache-hit rate. Compare the measured bottleneck with current quotas before changing a layer that wasn't the problem.",
          "text_sha256": "28d6296c8dd6b9253809e9d54c32a9acd7438f15b32620137b929122af9e147f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "28d6296c8dd6b9253809e9d54c32a9acd7438f15b32620137b929122af9e147f",
          "asset_sha256": "230c3d7994306eab379341bdc4f42bbec3c9d8a7868b7eddc8b027589a9ab87d"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "19",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m11p19-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "5e9bc93cc275ca382b799630cb6f66ecd29a8d1a25254e68b17d59c142f63b62",
        "2": "95c08dcb7244c22580e25446a537dcb76c6db50351c3d95e9db844556c246c0c",
        "3": "afe262a38a198c5526d60f8c1826e05d04c4426769d007d80340974f0d2c4502",
        "4": "de3eafebc77fa30adf43dbe0f26636da0df41204afd32c1069bbbf740d14c973"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s01-c1-1828fca70320",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A product record or log starts in the source. An ingestion path prepares it and indexes it in OpenSearch. The search A P I and dashboards then use that index rather than querying the source directly.",
          "text_sha256": "1828fca703203f20e21dc9949c29b672dbb08096da743dbacd08f085daad0f74",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "095b135d6337f30352c223fa893a6cdb4b447797e9ffc517f09259a89475e84b",
          "asset_sha256": "5e9bc93cc275ca382b799630cb6f66ecd29a8d1a25254e68b17d59c142f63b62"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s01-c2-7bb493c18036",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Because search uses a derived index, a source record can arrive before it is searchable. Choose the operating model, then plan access, retry and reindexing independently of source retention.",
          "text_sha256": "7bb493c1803616fd7740792aa7017def5947dc3e9727b12d8375001b3457c69b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7bb493c1803616fd7740792aa7017def5947dc3e9727b12d8375001b3457c69b",
          "asset_sha256": "5e9bc93cc275ca382b799630cb6f66ecd29a8d1a25254e68b17d59c142f63b62"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s02-c1-f1f1b4a47a0d",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Use a provisioned domain when you want to choose nodes, shards and other operating details. You gain control, and you still have to plan them.",
          "text_sha256": "f1f1b4a47a0d35250d439ba4f5b7d6599ae23019d5612a34a5922d3abee21ebe",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f1f1b4a47a0d35250d439ba4f5b7d6599ae23019d5612a34a5922d3abee21ebe",
          "asset_sha256": "95c08dcb7244c22580e25446a537dcb76c6db50351c3d95e9db844556c246c0c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s02-c2-3a098a48982a",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "With Serverless, choose a collection type for the job and let the service manage underlying capacity. Still check limits, access policies and cost for that collection.",
          "text_sha256": "3a098a48982a343ce2d20a7e3cf09b28d7f7d0823a7a1bc94c07f0010b968ec0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3a098a48982a343ce2d20a7e3cf09b28d7f7d0823a7a1bc94c07f0010b968ec0",
          "asset_sha256": "95c08dcb7244c22580e25446a537dcb76c6db50351c3d95e9db844556c246c0c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s02-c3-637971a66d4b",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Neither choice decides how a document should be mapped or fixes missing ingest. Design the query fields, measure indexing lag, and have a way to rebuild from the source.",
          "text_sha256": "637971a66d4b21353523192fba92b9207cc1dd6bda77f64d3def15a48c339f1e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "637971a66d4b21353523192fba92b9207cc1dd6bda77f64d3def15a48c339f1e",
          "asset_sha256": "95c08dcb7244c22580e25446a537dcb76c6db50351c3d95e9db844556c246c0c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s03-c1-0eb84eb7a8a9",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The event source sends records to a collector or ingestion pipeline. Transform them, manage buffering and protect credentials before the document reaches OpenSearch.",
          "text_sha256": "0eb84eb7a8a94d70805aca68998b437ae74deb1b1af7a1b23b04c439992de367",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0eb84eb7a8a94d70805aca68998b437ae74deb1b1af7a1b23b04c439992de367",
          "asset_sha256": "afe262a38a198c5526d60f8c1826e05d04c4426769d007d80340974f0d2c4502"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s03-c2-22ac92146252",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The index needs appropriate mappings, shards and retention. Monitor rejected documents and retry or recover them instead of assuming they reached the destination.",
          "text_sha256": "22ac92146252cc77e2d0880cfecdbb94ca3d30595b0fa38ef10706a40d0a4a41",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "22ac92146252cc77e2d0880cfecdbb94ca3d30595b0fa38ef10706a40d0a4a41",
          "asset_sha256": "afe262a38a198c5526d60f8c1826e05d04c4426769d007d80340974f0d2c4502"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s03-c3-af45935970a7",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Dashboards query and display what made it into the index. They do not collect logs or preserve the original source. Test the whole path from one emitted record to one searchable result.",
          "text_sha256": "af45935970a78a1904481555281e65b3ea05c513f429352ea0e723c0e1f96b2f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "af45935970a78a1904481555281e65b3ea05c513f429352ea0e723c0e1f96b2f",
          "asset_sha256": "afe262a38a198c5526d60f8c1826e05d04c4426769d007d80340974f0d2c4502"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s04-c1-bc8eafd3727c",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "The application writes the item to Dynamo D B and can read it from the table. That item A P I and a relevance-ranked search are two different paths.",
          "text_sha256": "bc8eafd3727c7cae646f20d5694b6fe50be885ae8cda146593bd13f53d6405cf",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1c84f4fdde1fa7ae0aea5e0d18c7b73726db99a79ea42f0f5a736d6c6098113a",
          "asset_sha256": "de3eafebc77fa30adf43dbe0f26636da0df41204afd32c1069bbbf740d14c973"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s04-c2-7c235adc974a",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Dynamo D B Streams triggers an indexer, which updates OpenSearch separately. A just-written item can exist in the table before search finds it. Handle change order, duplicates and deletes.",
          "text_sha256": "7c235adc974ac2b3627c2ffd791455f8f6f0ee9a168955db489b5205a1de6f7d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a0b4571832eeea6e66d21a87b94c7da921f39acb7e5dd4263d4e15a8b3452cac",
          "asset_sha256": "de3eafebc77fa30adf43dbe0f26636da0df41204afd32c1069bbbf740d14c973"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p19-andrew-exp-s04-c3-8f6a5a979274",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Measure consumer lag and indexing errors. If entries are absent or stale, backfill from the trusted source and check the search result afterward.",
          "text_sha256": "8f6a5a979274b47dc9eb365698b26fca8c059eda23981b55af707c544ae80a06",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8f6a5a979274b47dc9eb365698b26fca8c059eda23981b55af707c544ae80a06",
          "asset_sha256": "de3eafebc77fa30adf43dbe0f26636da0df41204afd32c1069bbbf740d14c973"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "21",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m11p21-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "1ddd144279daf88c4c25a7938b2ec8d1421759df0a5a9a1d662175aa81dbe772",
        "2": "dadd0d98874322f802ddf21fae45ddc470c9025670fd712217697359c2d8a383",
        "3": "77916a8da67593d39dced55140902ef4e38d1182447c84b6ce5b42e7eb7f5764"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p21-andrew-exp-s01-c1-b10d28901c72",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The app uses a compatible driver and works with Jason-like documents. In this instance-based example the primary and readers share distributed cluster storage. Choose the topology for the application's reads and availability.",
          "text_sha256": "b10d28901c72c32984ac4ba37ed28f7f7ef640e928732f0aefd5bcf9b901cf9d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0bb860e4acc1804f5a014209fa36ed921631773e41a8b1231ca52e832d1152b4",
          "asset_sha256": "1ddd144279daf88c4c25a7938b2ec8d1421759df0a5a9a1d662175aa81dbe772"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p21-andrew-exp-s01-c2-b0a2902d1a5b",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Support for selected MongoDB APIs does not mean identical behavior. Test the actual driver, query operators and indexes against the deployment and engine version you plan to use.",
          "text_sha256": "b0a2902d1a5b1c02e23c01b9d82199c5210949334bb4a77c66153affa0cad23d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b0a2902d1a5b1c02e23c01b9d82199c5210949334bb4a77c66153affa0cad23d",
          "asset_sha256": "1ddd144279daf88c4c25a7938b2ec8d1421759df0a5a9a1d662175aa81dbe772"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p21-andrew-exp-s02-c1-b08b6dadc044",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Can this MongoDB app move unchanged? Test its drivers, authentication, queries, indexes and transactions on the target. Include failover and measure latency against what the app needs.",
          "text_sha256": "b08b6dadc044e0e2e60de3aaad38709344bcb91f782818dc2e534325270999e1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b08b6dadc044e0e2e60de3aaad38709344bcb91f782818dc2e534325270999e1",
          "asset_sha256": "dadd0d98874322f802ddf21fae45ddc470c9025670fd712217697359c2d8a383"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p21-andrew-exp-s02-c2-f1a6a96b34b5",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "In the instance-based example the primary handles writes. Replica reads depend on the chosen setup and can lag. Engine version and deployment type affect what is supported, so do not extrapolate this one picture to every deployment.",
          "text_sha256": "f1a6a96b34b579fd38d0701732a8878cea6fa38757884971ba3ea9f2b2aaf74f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f1a6a96b34b579fd38d0701732a8878cea6fa38757884971ba3ea9f2b2aaf74f",
          "asset_sha256": "dadd0d98874322f802ddf21fae45ddc470c9025670fd712217697359c2d8a383"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p21-andrew-exp-s03-c1-7bf7a403f81d",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "With Standard storage, compare instance and storage charges plus request I O. Measure a representative workload; a read-heavy app can change the cost balance.",
          "text_sha256": "7bf7a403f81d6ca85e76f6185f4ad595f078d67376e9ee61c9f96844cc40690f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6fa1ec4596a6fb034af438185887a565db97b53789854a18989692fd6a551ac4",
          "asset_sha256": "77916a8da67593d39dced55140902ef4e38d1182447c84b6ce5b42e7eb7f5764"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p21-andrew-exp-s03-c2-56595c6a1672",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "In supported instance-based clusters, I O-Optimized removes the per-I O operation charge, but instances and storage still cost money. Compare the total instead of assuming one setup is always cheaper.",
          "text_sha256": "56595c6a1672dee7c09dd8ebef853d2753a95882b25994563c4ea8a898f708a8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1ab7ded6946f816ea533d728a097dcdcea24c36676dbaa33c769b386613e2dc9",
          "asset_sha256": "77916a8da67593d39dced55140902ef4e38d1182447c84b6ce5b42e7eb7f5764"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p21-andrew-exp-s03-c3-60ba7d679285",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Include replicas, backup storage, data transfer and growth. Check current regional prices against measured work, not just the I O line item.",
          "text_sha256": "60ba7d679285203f39b7a01152fbc7d98b6b9f1a1d2291d12fb59b32c041b8a6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7ed582a9569ed2cc0da027b0c63f4cc3bcd959f456cfa373a55fd71add6d270f",
          "asset_sha256": "77916a8da67593d39dced55140902ef4e38d1182447c84b6ce5b42e7eb7f5764"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
